# Team Operating Procedure: how a request becomes shipped code

Goal: many specialised sub-agent teams work in parallel on one project **without** client/developer
misunderstandings, cross-team conflicts, or rework. Everything is decided on paper (docs, wireframes,
contracts) and **approved by a person before code is written**. This file is the single source of terms.

> Rule zero: **no code starts until the Planning Gate (G3) is signed.** Every later change that is not in the
> signed docs goes back through a Change Request (CR), never "just do it".

---

## 0. Glossary (use only these words, so nobody means two things)

| Term | Exactly means |
|---|---|
| **Client** | The person who owns the requirement and signs the gates. |
| **Lead** | The main agent. Talks to the Client, dispatches teams, owns the task map. Never writes feature code. |
| **Team** | A named group of sub-agents with one job and one set of files (section 3). A team never edits another team's files. |
| **Sub-agent** | One agent definition (`.claude/agents/<name>.md`) inside a team. Has its own session, tools, skills. |
| **Slug** | Short kebab-case id of one request, e.g. `agent-settings`. All its docs live in `docs/team/plans/<slug>/`. |
| **Phase** | A big stage of the procedure (P0..P6). Ends at a Gate. |
| **Gate (G0..G6)** | A stop point where a person says APPROVE or CHANGES. Nothing crosses a gate unsigned. |
| **Goal** | An outcome the Client can see ("settings page works"). Has 2-6 tasks. |
| **Task (T1..)** | The smallest unit one sub-agent does in one worktree. Has owner, files, depends-on, acceptance. |
| **Wave** | Tasks with no dependency between them, run in parallel. Wave 2 starts when wave 1 is merged. |
| **Contract** | Shared, signed shape between teams: types, API request/response, DB columns, events. FE and BE both code against it. |
| **Wireframe** | Layout drawing with **named components** (section 6). Not a mood board. |
| **Component ID** | Stable name of a UI piece, `PageName.Region.Component` (e.g. `Settings.Header.SaveButton`). Used in every doc and ticket. |
| **Mock** | Fake data/store that lets FE work before BE is ready; removed at the integration phase. |
| **Lock** | A claim on a file or resource (section 8) so two agents never edit it at once. |
| **Loophole / Hustle / Conflict** | Plan defects the Detector must find (section 5): a gap, an overlap/duplicate effort, a contradiction. |
| **CR (Change Request)** | Written change to a signed doc. Needs the same gate the doc passed. |
| **Done** | Acceptance criteria met, QA = APPROVE, screenshot attached, committed on its branch. Not "it compiles". |

