## 1. The procedure at a glance

```
Client request
   |
P0 INTAKE ──G0──> P1 DISCOVERY ──G1──> P2 UX & WIREFRAME ──G2──> P3 ARCHITECTURE & TASK SPLIT
                                                                        |
                                              P3b DETECTOR (loophole / conflict / hustle) ──G3 PLAN SIGNED──┐
                                                                                                          |
        P4 BUILD (waves, per goal)  <──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          BE ║ FE ║ Design ║ Docs/Blog   (parallel, own worktrees)
          each task: build -> QA -> screenshot -> commit            ──G4 per goal (Client sees it)
                |
        P5 INTEGRATE & TEST (remove mocks, e2e, browser QA)          ──G5
                |
        P6 RELEASE & DOCS (changelog, user docs, handoff to a person)──G6
```

Why it avoids conflict: **one owner per file**, **contracts before code**, **wireframes before UI**,
**detector before split**, **screenshot before "done"**, **a person commits and deploys** (see project CLAUDE.md).

