## 3. Teams (each is a "# subAgent" group: separate unit, separate owner, separate files)

| Team | Members (sub-agents) | Owns (only these) | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Planning Team** | explorer, ux-lead, architect, planner, plan-auditor | `docs/team/plans/<slug>/*` | P1-P3b |
| **Design / UI Team** | ux-designer, ui-designer, design-system-keeper | wireframes, theme tokens, `components/ui` look only | P2, P4 |
| **Build Team: BE** | backend-dev (+ db-migrator) | API, DB schema, jobs, services | P4 |
| **Build Team: FE** | frontend-dev (+ state-store dev) | pages, components, store, API client | P4 |
| **QA Team** | qa-reviewer, browser-tester, a11y-checker | tests, screenshots, review reports | P4-P5 |
| **Docs Team** | user-docs-writer (Main page, User/API docs), api-doc-writer | `content/docs`, OpenAPI text, README | P4, P6 |
| **Blog / Content Team** | blogger | blog posts, release notes, landing copy | P6 |
| **Game-Assets Team** (only for game projects) | sprite, animation, engine agents (section 7) | `assets/`, game scripts | on demand |
| **Lead (main agent)** | the lead | task map, merges, gates, Client talk | all |

Team rules:
- A team **reads** everything, **writes** only what it owns. Need a change elsewhere? Post an **ESCALATE** (to Architect, one-way, written).
- Teams talk through documents and contracts, not through each other's code.
- Teams of one gate run in **parallel**; the Lead merges.

