## 4. Documents and standard names (one file name = one purpose)

All in `docs/team/plans/<slug>/`, numbered by phase so order is obvious:

```
00_brief.md            request, scope, out-of-scope, success check      (Lead)
01_discovery.md        reuse list, risks, constraints                   (Explorer)
02_ux.md               flows, states, component inventory               (UX)
02_wireframes/         <Page>.<n>-<state>.md|svg|html  e.g. Settings.1-empty.md
02_prototype.html      clickable artifact (CDN React/Tailwind), Client signs
03_design.md           architecture, pseudo code, ownership             (Architect)
03_contracts/          types.ts, api.md (OpenAPI), events.md
03_db.md               ER diagram + migration notes
03_tasks.md            goals -> tasks DAG                               (Planner)
03b_audit.md           loophole / conflict / hustle report              (Plan-Auditor)
04_reports/Tn.md       per task: what changed, files, screenshot link   (Dev)
05_qa.md               test results, wireframe-vs-live diff              (QA)
06_release.md          changelog, docs links, handoff                   (Docs)
CR_<n>.md              change requests
```

Diagram standards (use text-first so they diff in git):
| Need | Format | File |
|---|---|---|
| DB relations | Mermaid `erDiagram` | `03_db.md` |
| UX flow | Mermaid `flowchart` (screen -> action -> screen) | `02_ux.md` |
| Code / call flow | Mermaid `sequenceDiagram` | `03_design.md` |
| State of a component | Mermaid `stateDiagram-v2` | `02_ux.md` |
| Layout | ASCII wireframe or HTML artifact | `02_wireframes/` |

Naming: files `snake_case` with phase number; Component IDs `PascalCase.Dotted`; task ids `T1..`; branches `wt-<slug>-T<n>`;
data `snake_case` (project rule); commits Conventional Commits.

