## 6. Wireframe-first confirmation (avoid "you changed the wrong page")

Problem: the Client says "change the button" and the agent edits the wrong page/component.
Fix: **never describe a UI change in words; point at a Component ID on a wireframe.**

1. Every page has a wireframe with named components and a numbered click map:
   ```
   Settings (route /settings)                       state: default
   +--------------------------------------------------+
   | [Settings.Header.Title]      [Settings.Header.SaveButton] |
   | [Settings.Tabs.General | Agents | Builder]                |
   | [Settings.Form.NameInput]                                |
   +--------------------------------------------------+
   Click map: Settings.Header.SaveButton -> PUT /api/v1/settings -> toast "Saved" -> stay on page
   States: default, loading, empty, error, saving, success
   ```
2. **Locate before edit**: the dev agent must print `Component ID -> file:line` and the current screenshot, and the Client (or Lead) confirms "yes, that one".
3. **Prototype first**: build the screen as an artifact page (CDN React + Tailwind, mock data). Client clicks it. Expected behaviour is written next to each click. Only then does real FE work start.
4. **Verify after**: browser-tester opens the real page, clicks each item in the click map, screenshots each state, diffs against the wireframe. Any mismatch = CHANGES.
5. Anything the Client mentions that is **not in the wireframe** (a related page or layout) triggers a CR and a wireframe update first.

