  # ---------- Game-Assets Team (only when the project is a game) ----------
  game_assets_builder:
    bit_sprite_agent:   { tools: [Read, Write, Bash], skills: [], plugins: [],
                          job: "pixel sprites/tilesets (e.g. Aseprite CLI, or generated PNG sheets), palette + size spec" }
    animation_agent:    { tools: [Read, Write, Bash], job: "frame lists, sprite-sheet JSON, easing; previews as GIF" }
    godot_agent:        { tools: [Read, Grep, Edit, Write, Bash], job: "GDScript/scenes, headless export + tests" }
    unity_agent:        { tools: [Read, Grep, Edit, Write, Bash], job: "C# scripts/scenes, batchmode build + tests" }
```

Rules for the list:
- Browser: **claude-in-chrome** for real clicks and screenshots on a visible page; **playwright** (`bun run test:e2e`) for repeatable scripted tests. Never trigger alert/confirm dialogs.
- Web search (WebSearch / context7) is for the Planning Team and Blogger only; Dev agents work from the signed docs.
- Project rules always apply: no `git commit`/push/deploy by agents unless the Client asks, never print secrets, `bun` not `bunx`.
- To pick better agents: ask `explorer` + a web search for "best practice agent teams" and add the finding to `handbook/`.

