## 9. Conflict-prevention rules (the short list)

1. One owner per file per wave. Two tasks needing one file are merged or serialised by the Planner.
2. Contract first: change a contract = CR + both sides notified; code never "adapts quietly".
3. Client words become Component IDs and acceptance criteria before work starts.
4. Scope creep goes to a CR. The Lead answers "later / next goal / CR", never silently adds.
5. Escalation path: Dev -> Architect (design question) -> Lead -> Client (scope question). Never skip upward.
6. Every task ends with evidence (screenshot or test output) in `04_reports/Tn.md`.
7. Mocks are labelled `MOCK:` and listed in `04_reports`; P5 fails while any remain.
8. Small commits per task; a person decides what goes to the shared branch.

## 10. Roles of the Client (what we need from you, and when)

| Gate | You decide | You see |
|---|---|---|
| G0 | scope, out-of-scope | brief |
| G2 | the look and the click behaviour | clickable prototype |
| G3 | goals and their order | task map + audit result |
| G4 | each goal OK / changes | screenshots per goal |
| G6 | accept | release note + docs |

Goal template (what the Planner fills):
```
goals:
  goal1: { outcome: "...", tasks: [T1, T2, T3], gate: G4, wave: 1 }
  goal2: { outcome: "...", tasks: [T4, T5, T6], gate: G4, wave: 2 }
```

